        <groundspeak:log id="683859284">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-05T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="70898">Tommi Potx</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;Mission to Lethbridge

BCP286; With the archiving of GC43F3, there was no way I could not go on one last cap binge. RIP, GC43F3

TFTC; it has been a good run.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681468025">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1298988">dronnord</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP286 Lethbridge&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;N49° 39.816 W112° 48.818&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we were walking alongside the house next tot he walkway i was watching the home owner walking around inside his house watching us. I was taken with his Arizona Landscaping and took a few photos of it for my own projects. This must of been the last straw for snoopy roger because he couldn`t contain himself. He marched out onto his front step and demanded to know what I was doing. I wanted to tell him I was from Home &amp; Gardens and we had just excluded his home from this months magazine..but I decided to just tell him the truth that i liked his Az landscaping. He smiled and waved...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adventures are always funner after the fact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cap # 20  today&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681184678">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP286 - Lethbridge

&lt;strong&gt;Posted:&lt;/strong&gt;  N49° 39.815' W112° 48.814'

&lt;strong&gt;My GPSr:&lt;/strong&gt;  N49° 39.816' W112° 48.818'&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After parking we made our way via a walkway - admiring the landscaping in front the nearby house - and found the cap on the edge of a slope that offered a wonderful vista of the valley below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680229852">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4853503">gumbyphv</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;I found BCP286 Lethbridge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driving to this cap next I passed quite a few people outside enjoying the evening and I also passed a lot of nice houses.  I found some convenient parking with a nice path right out to the cap.  Looked at my GPS to see that I was getting close looked down and spotted the cap.  Another nice view from another great cap.  TFTBC  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
